- How would you adapt if costs were a non-linear function cost(s) instead of s? 
- How would you extend to count the number of ways to reach n with min cost, not just the cost itself?

## Why This Is Asked

Models real build/dependency graphs where costs accumulate; asks for both memoized and tabular DP to compare patterns and understand trade-offs. Emphasizes modulo arithmetic and edge-case handling for unreachable sinks and tight budgets.

## Key Concepts

- DP on DAG with an extra weight dimension
